# oracle: compute pe/atom and stress/atom (pair and kspace terms) with kspace_style esp and pair coul/esp (the w244es_ortho system), after 10 nve steps, per-atom values dumped; as native, the per-atom kspace virial has the vg term only, not the vg2 term of the global virial
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 4.5e-15, atoms 1.9e-14.
# oracle-files: w268es_peratom.dump
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 abs=1e-10 filerel=1e-10
units           real
atom_style      charge
boundary        p p p
lattice         fcc 5.64
region          box block 0 4 0 5 0 3
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box basis 1 1 basis 2 1 basis 3 2 basis 4 2
mass            * 22.99
set             type 1 charge 1.0
set             type 2 charge -1.0
displace_atoms  all random 0.1 0.1 0.1 4411 units box
velocity        all create 300 8812 loop geom
pair_style      coul/esp 8.0
pair_coeff      * *
kspace_style    esp 1e-4
fix             1 all nve
timestep        1.0
compute         pk all pe/atom kspace
compute         sk all stress/atom NULL kspace
compute         pp all pe/atom pair
compute         sp all stress/atom NULL pair
thermo_style    custom step pe ecoul elong press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g norm no
thermo          5
run             10
write_dump      all custom w268es_peratom.dump id c_pk c_sk[1] c_sk[2] c_sk[3] c_sk[4] c_sk[5] c_sk[6] c_pp c_sp[1] c_sp[2] c_sp[3] c_sp[4] c_sp[5] c_sp[6] modify format float %.15g sort id
